codex.bin, gemini.bin and opencode.bin are raw PTY recordings (120x40) of the
startup screens of Codex CLI 0.160.0, Gemini CLI 0.62.0 and opencode 1.18.34,
made without accounts (dummy API keys only), for screen-detection tests; see
crates/runner/tests/detect.rs and crates/detect/tests/emulated.rs.

htop.bin and nvim.bin are raw PTY recordings (120x40) of htop 3.5.3 (`htop -d 10`)
and Neovim 0.12.2 (editing /etc/os-release past a stale swap file, then :vsplit),
made in a clean alpine:3 container as user `dev` on host `box` (home /home/dev),
for the emulator snapshot tests (crates/emu/tests/recordings.rs). The htop
header (CPU count, memory, load, uptime) is the recording host's.

claude-busy-120x40.bin and claude-busy-50x20.bin are raw PTY recordings of
Claude Code v2.1.296 in its classic (main screen) mode
(CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_ALTERNATE_SCREEN=1) at 120x40 and 50x20, six turns each
against a local stand-in for the Messages API (no account): long streamed
Markdown answers and a Bash tool call printing 150 lines, with one resize.
claude-fullscreen-120x40.bin is the same session in Claude Code's default
full-screen mode (alternate screen, mouse tracking). All text in them is the
stand-in's; the working directory is /work. Used by the emulator history tests
(crates/emu/tests/history.rs).

claude.bin is a raw PTY recording (120x40) of Claude Code v2.1.288's idle
prompt box. Two banner strings were replaced after recording: the working
directory (now `~/work`) and the plan name (now `Claude API`).
